# Scratch queue rows HCS (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/HCS.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-HCS Hearth crow swap: spawn crash fix, H&H crow, nest spawning, tree and roof nests, 2026-11-10 ([plan_hearth_crow_swap.md](../plan_hearth_crow_swap.md) section 8, TODO `creativedelight/members #54`, `largecontent/mod-additions #60`)
@@date 2026-11-10
@@jars creativedelight
@@sources feature_writeup/plan_hearth_crow_swap.md
@@prep spawn-animals=true
@@prep toml hearthandharvest-common.toml crow stealChance 1.0
@@prep toml hearthandharvest-common.toml crow carryTicks 200
@@prep toml loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
@@text
@@text Jars: Creative Delight and Creative Common built 2026-11-10, NOT installed (the game was running). Install both, then run. SQ-HH-401 to -502 and CQ-HH-401 to -405 were rewritten 2026-11-10 for `hearthandharvest:crow` (note in that section); run them with this set. Fixture for SQ-HCS-09: a 1.2.02 save with a tamed AM crow, an AM crow carrying an item and a generated ground nest.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-HCS-01 | fresh normal world boots past spawn prep with no crow scan errors
@group B
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@commands Fresh normal world (default type, random seed); boot to `Done`; `shell grep -c "out of bound" logs/latest.log`; `shell grep -c "Exception generating new chunk" logs/latest.log`; `shell grep -c "CrowEvents" logs/latest.log`
@pass Reaches `Done`; all three counts 0
@fails Crash report under `crash-reports/`; a scan left in `hearth/crow/CrowEvents` or `nest/`
@from batches/r1111/b1.qb
bootexpect Done \(
shell for p in "out of bound" "Exception generating new chunk" "CrowEvents"; do echo "$p: $(grep -c "$p" logs/latest.log)"; done; ls crash-reports 2>/dev/null | head
# KubeJS recipe parse warnings excluded since r1118 (judge-8, 2026-11-18): 15 'Index 0 out of bounds' lines from recipe parsing, none from chunk gen
bootreject ^(?!.*KubeJS Recipe Event).*out of bound
bootreject Exception generating new chunk
bootreject CrowEvents

## SQ-HCS-02 | 40 new chunks of forest and plains by bot, no long tick naming crow code
@phase worldgen
@group B
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@commands Same boot: `/tp` through 40 new chunks of forest and plains (`zq` path or 40 `tp` steps of 128 blocks); watch tick times
@pass No crash; no tick over 200 ms naming `Crow`, `Nest` or `RoofNests` in the log or a JFR hot method
@fails `RoofNests.decorate` or `NestCrows` in the profile: the structure-start read or an entity query is too wide
@from batches/r1111/b1.qb
> locate biome minecraft:forest
waitlog (nearest minecraft:forest is at|Could not find) 600
capture FO nearest minecraft:forest is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> pbot spawn hcs2 {FO1} 150 {FO3}
> effect give hcs2 minecraft:slow_falling 600 0 true
> effect give hcs2 minecraft:resistance 600 4 true
repeat 20
> execute as hcs2 at @s run tp @s ~128 150 ~
sleep 3
end
> locate biome minecraft:plains
waitlog (nearest minecraft:plains is at|Could not find) 600
capture PL nearest minecraft:plains is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp hcs2 {PL1} 150 {PL3}
repeat 20
> execute as hcs2 at @s run tp @s ~ 150 ~128
sleep 3
end
> pbot remove hcs2
reject (?i)Exception.*(Crow|Nest|RoofNests)
shell grep -nE "Can't keep up" logs/latest.log | tail -5; grep -nE "Exception|ERROR" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "crow|nest" | head -5
look no Can't keep up during the walk worth attention; no crow / nest exception (JFR hot methods checked after the run)

## SQ-HCS-03 | Chunky 30 x 30 chunks of forest: nests on leaves, about 1 in 6 chunks
@phase long
@group B
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@commands Chunky 30 x 30 chunks in `minecraft:forest` (seed with a large forest); then a script or `/cdevfind hearthandharvest:nest` count over the area
@pass Every nest sits on leaves with nothing above; count near 150 (1 in 6 chunks, about 100 to 200); none on grass or the ground
@fails No nests: biome tag `creativedelight:crow_nest_forests` empty or modifier `nest_tree_top` not loaded (`/cdevplace` the placed feature); nests on the ground: heightmap in `placed_feature/nest_tree_top.json`
@from batches/r1111/b1.qb
# FO located here (r1124fx runner-1, 2026-11-24): SQ-HCS-02, which captured it, is not in the selection
> locate biome minecraft:forest
waitlog (nearest minecraft:forest is at|Could not find) 600
capture FO nearest minecraft:forest is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> chunky world minecraft:overworld
> chunky shape square
> chunky center {FO1} {FO3}
> chunky radius 240
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
> save-all flush
sleep 10
shell python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/region_blocks.py blocks @ 'hearthandharvest:nest' --box $(( {FO1} - 240 )) $(( {FO3} - 240 )) $(( {FO1} + 240 )) $(( {FO3} + 240 )) --near 'leaves' 2>&1 | tail -40
look nest count about 100 to 200 over the 900 chunks of the forest square, every nest with a leaves neighbour and depth 0 (top block), none on grass

